{#
  ABOUT ME — Figma 664:61547 (desktop layout) and 666:61738 (mobile, scrolled).

  A PARALLAX, AND THE TWO NODES ARE ITS TWO ENDS. 664:61547 is the resting state:
  the photo in a rounded box at the top of the band, the summary below it, every
  line muted. 666:61738 is where it arrives: the photo dimmed and full-bleed with
  the summary sitting over it in white. Neither node is the whole thing — the
  section is the travel between them.

  THREE LAYERS, AND ONLY THE MIDDLE ONE MOVES.
    .about__media    the photo, position:sticky, pinned while the band scrolls
    .about__summary  the text and the clock, translated up over it by transform
    .about__runway   an empty block that buys the pin its scroll distance
  scripts/about-parallax.js writes one custom property, --about-progress, and
  everything above reads it. It writes no layout — see the note in that file.

  THE CLOCK IS THE EXISTING COMPONENT, MOVED AND NOT REBUILT. Every data-clock-*
  hook below is byte-identical to what scripts/clock.js already binds, so that
  file needed no edit: the live Amsterdam time, the three rotating hands and the
  time-of-day status schedule all keep working exactly as before. The comp's
  "01:51 / Probably in deep work" is one moment of that schedule, not a string to
  hardcode — and not even a consistent one, since 01:51 falls in the block that
  says "probably asleep".

  ONE THING IS NEW IN THIS MARKUP: the "At" label before the time. 666:61759
  draws it as its own text node, Body Medium against the time's Title Large, so
  it is a span here rather than something CSS could fake.

  #about-me AND data-header-theme STAY ON THIS ELEMENT. The id is the nav anchor
  and the target analytics-events.js observes for view_about; the theme attribute
  is what the header reads, and about-parallax.js flips it to dark as the photo
  darkens so the header does not sit light-on-light over the end state.
#}

<section class="about" id="about-me" data-header-theme="light">

  {#- ONE STICKY STAGE, BOTH LAYERS INSIDE IT. The photo and the summary used to
      be two independent sticky elements, and that is what broke the exit: their
      pins were bounded by the same container but started at different offsets,
      so the summary un-stuck roughly 560px before the photo did and slid off the
      top on its own. Pinning the pair as one unit means beat 2 is free — when
      the stage releases, the image and the content leave together because they
      are the same element. -#}
  <div class="about__stage">

  {#- The photo. aria-hidden with an empty alt: it is atmosphere, and the three
      paragraphs beside it already say everything it says. -#}
  <div class="about__media" aria-hidden="true">
    <img
      class="about__photo"
      src="{{ about.photo.file }}"
      alt=""
      width="1600"
      height="2844"
      decoding="async"
      draggable="false"
    />
    <div class="about__media-dim"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="about__summary">
    <div class="about__inner">

      <div class="about__content">
        <h2 class="about__heading">
          <span class="about__heading-lead">{{ about.heading.lead }}</span>
          <span class="about__heading-rest">{{ about.heading.rest }}</span>
        </h2>

        {#- RUNS, NOT A STRING. about.bio is a list of lists, so the emphasis the
            node specifies lives in the data. The whitespace control is
            load-bearing: the runs carry their own spaces and must be joined with
            nothing between them. The bold runs are what go white first. -#}
        {%- for para in about.bio %}
          <p class="about__bio">
            {%- for run in para -%}
              {%- if run.bold %}<strong>{{ run.text }}</strong>{% else %}{{ run.text }}{% endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </p>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>

      <div class="about__clock" data-clock>
        <div class="about__clock-face">
          <svg
            class="about__clock-hands"
            viewBox="-22.3 -3.9 118 105.8"
            fill="none"
            aria-hidden="true"
            focusable="false"
          >
            {#- THE VIEWBOX IS OFFSET, NOT REDRAWN. clock.js pins PIVOT = "52 30"
                and rotates the hands about it, so those coordinates cannot move.
                Shifting the window instead (-22.3, -3.9) puts that same pivot at
                63% across and 32% down of the 90.5 x 81.14 box, which is where
                666:61719 has the hub, and 118 x 105.8 matches the box's aspect so
                nothing letterboxes. -#}
            <defs>
              {#- Along each hand's own length, dark at the hub and light at the
                  tip. userSpaceOnUse so the gradient rotates WITH the hand — a
                  transform on the line carries its paint with it. Two of them
                  because the hands are different lengths and one shared ramp
                  would leave the shorter hand's tip mid-gradient. -#}
              <linearGradient id="about-clock-hour" x1="52" y1="30" x2="52" y2="-9"
                              gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
                <stop offset="0" stop-color="#8A8A8A" />
                <stop offset="1" stop-color="#DADADA" />
              </linearGradient>
              <linearGradient id="about-clock-minute" x1="52" y1="30" x2="52" y2="-17"
                              gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
                <stop offset="0" stop-color="#8A8A8A" />
                <stop offset="1" stop-color="#DADADA" />
              </linearGradient>
            </defs>

            <line class="about__clock-hand about__clock-hand--hour" data-clock-hour
                  x1="52" y1="30" x2="52" y2="-9" />
            <line class="about__clock-hand about__clock-hand--minute" data-clock-minute
                  x1="52" y1="30" x2="52" y2="-17" />
            {#- The only hand that crosses the pivot: it runs a little past the hub
                on the far side, as 666:61719 draws it. -#}
            <line class="about__clock-hand about__clock-hand--second" data-clock-second
                  x1="52" y1="43" x2="52" y2="-33" />
            <circle class="about__clock-hub" cx="52" cy="30" r="6.5" />
          </svg>
          <p class="about__clock-time">
            <span class="about__clock-at">{{ about.clock.at }}</span>
            <span class="about__clock-value" data-clock-time>{{ about.clock.time }}</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="about__clock-body">
        <p class="about__clock-status">
          <span class="about__clock-lead" data-clock-lead>{{ about.clock.statusLead }}</span>
          <span class="about__clock-headline" data-clock-status>{{ about.clock.status }}</span>
        </p>
        <p class="about__clock-detail" data-clock-detail>{{ about.clock.detail }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  </div>{#- /.about__stage -#}

  {#- THE PIN'S SCROLL DISTANCE. A real element for the same reason .hero__runway
      and .work__runway are: padding sits outside the content box a sticky child
      is bounded by, so only a sibling with height can extend the pin. -#}
  <div class="about__runway" aria-hidden="true"></div>
</section>
